      "replacements": [
        {
          "from": "**Yes** \u2192 **`/to-spec`** (turn the thread into a spec), then **`/to-tickets`** to split it into tracer-bullet tickets, each declaring its **blocking edges**.",
          "to": "**Yes** \u2192 optionally use **`/to-spec`** to capture the thread as Markdown, then **`/implement-spec`** from that spec or the agreed conversation. Use **`/to-tickets`** only if the user explicitly wants ticket tracking."
        },
        {
          "from": "It reads the tickets as a **task graph**",
          "to": "It derives work dependencies from the spec or plan"
        },
        {
          "from": "**`/setup-matt-pocock-skills`**: run before your first engineering flow to configure the issue tracker, triage labels, and doc layout the other skills assume. Custom issue trackers also work.",
          "to": "**`/setup-matt-pocock-skills`**: use only when explicitly choosing tracker-based workflows that need configuration. Ordinary implementation and review need no tickets, labels or tracker setup."
        },
        {
          "from": "Then work the tickets one of two ways:",
          "to": "If ticket tracking was explicitly chosen, work the tickets one of two ways:"
        }
      ]
    },
